{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-5-5","id":"msg_011CgtPeCZfLYwxbgrGDXcgK","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The system prompt is now split into two cache-marked blocks, so a `save_fact` write should only re-cache the small per-athlete block. There is one open risk: the static block may be too small to cache at all.\n\n**The change** (`bot.py`, `build_system`): the static `INSTRUCTIONS` text is its own block with a cache marker, and comes first. The per-athlete block (date, profile, zones, goal, facts, language) follows, with its own marker. Only that second block changes on `save_fact` or at midnight. Tools, the tool loop and fact storage are unchanged.\n\n**Verification:** I ran a fake-LLM test against temp copies of the data and log files, so the real `logs/usage.jsonl` and `data/athletes.json` were not touched. The static block was byte-identical before and after a `save_fact` and on the next day, and the new fact appeared in the athlete block. I made no real API calls, so the cache behaviour is not verified live.\n\n**Open risk:** caching needs at least 1024 tokens in the prefix on Sonnet models. My estimate (not the Claude tokenizer) is about 830 tokens for the tool schemas plus static instructions. If that holds, the static marker is silently ignored and the fix only partly works. Adding roughly 200 tokens of real instruction content would fix it. I did not pad the text with filler, since the coaching rules are your call. The check on the next deploy: after a `save_fact`, `cache_creation_input_tokens` should be about the size of the athlete block (~200), not the whole prompt (~1000+).\n\n**Colleague's note:** I applied the two-marker split with static text first, byte-stable static content, keeping all facts loaded, and using the usage fields to diagnose. Tool filtering was already in place and I left it alone. Their figures and Telegram details don't apply here. ANSWER.md has the full list.\n\nNothing is committed. The changes are in `bot.py` and the new `ANSWER.md`."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2328,"cache_read_input_tokens":44098,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2328},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a5d6de8f-7299-49ea-9eb4-4ceadd95f17e","uuid":"5810c769-b7cf-4bd1-8d41-4bfcfafae612","timestamp":"2026-11-10T01:37:09.866Z","request_id":"req_011CgtPeCEJnZkpPTwivUSCX"}
